+/* The four hot float ops, four lanes at once (x86-64 with SSE4.1 + FMA, the
+ * lifted code's TJ_PPU_HOST_SIMD build). Bit-identical to the scalar
+ * vmx_ref_* above, which stay the reference (tests/test_ppu_vmx_simd.c): the
+ * ops are lane-wise, so lanes stay in memory order and only each word's bytes
+ * are swapped; the host computes in the same IEEE single precision with
+ * round-to-nearest (MXCSR default, no FTZ/DAZ) as the scalar code, FMA is
+ * fused like fmaf(), and NaN precedence, the default NaN and the NJ flush are
+ * applied with masks exactly as vmx_vnan2 / vmx_fix / vmx_flush do.
+ * vnmsubfp is -(a*c - b), NOT fnmadd's -(a*c) + b: the two differ in the sign
+ * of an exact zero. */
